  "description": "Our All-Road frame was designed for the rider that wants to travel anywhere. Designed for long comfortable days in the saddle with stable relaxed geometry. Built to last generations, with versatility to allow for a wide range of drivetrain, wheel, and fork options. With tire capacity up to 45 mm, it will handle any terrain, paved or unpaved.\n\nThe All-Road features a comfortably low bottom bracket, longer headtube, and size specific chainstays for stability. Braze-ons include rack mounts, fender mounts, and three water bottle mounts (two on the 44 and 47cm). Thanks to a brushed finish, this frame will be pleasing to the eye and a cinch to maintain for generations with a simple Scotchbrite pad. And you’ll be rolling ’til your dying day with our lifetime warranty and crash replacement policy!\n\nWith 11 sizes ranging from 44cm to 64cm, there is an All-Road frame for nearly every rider. The smaller 44 cm and 47 cm frames are based on 26″ wheels, and can use 650b tires with narrower tires. We do this to reduce the toe overlap, which can be a problem with smaller frames and larger tires. Each frame comes with the rider’s choice of Paragon sliding dropout inserts which will allow for a wide variety of axle types, including thru-axle and Rohloff.\n\nThe All-Road is well-suited to gravel riding, but if that’s your primary use then check out our purpose-built gravel frame, the Conestoga.\n\nWanted to use rim brakes? Travel couplings? No worries, the All-Road is completely customizable with applicable upcharges and lead times.",
